From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:27:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: apple,jpeg: DMA window only for 32-bit
 engines

T8140's JPEG engines take 64-bit buffer addresses, so they use their
DART's full window. Keep apple,dma-range required for T6041, whose engine
has 32-bit pointer registers, and disallow it elsewhere.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0a51296919a866637a4f312d486c6d5a7906be50)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/apple,jpeg.yaml | 20 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,jpeg.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,jpeg.yaml
index 5e31390cf9..839d29392c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,jpeg.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,jpeg.yaml
@@ -15,9 +15,9 @@ description: |
   share a power domain. The power controller manages the gate; no separate
   clock or firmware interface is required.
 
-  The DMA window reserves one 4 GiB slice of the DART high alias. The engine
-  has 32-bit buffer pointer registers; use of this alias for jobs still needs
-  hardware qualification on each compatible.
+  On T6041 the DMA window reserves one 4 GiB slice of the DART high alias for
+  the engine's 32-bit buffer pointer registers. T8140 engines take 64-bit
+  buffer addresses and use their DART's full window.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ properties:
       - const: 0x10000000000
       - const: 0x100000000
     description: Device-visible DMA window, as a 64-bit base and size.
+      Only for engines with 32-bit buffer pointers.
 
 required:
   - compatible
@@ -50,7 +51,18 @@ required:
   - interrupts
   - iommus
   - power-domains
-  - apple,dma-range
+
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: apple,t6041-jpeg
+    then:
+      required:
+        - apple,dma-range
+    else:
+      properties:
+        apple,dma-range: false
 
 additionalProperties: false
 
